# =============================================================================
# Build context allowlist for workflow/containers/Dockerfile.
# =============================================================================
#
# DENY EVERYTHING, THEN NAME WHAT MAY ENTER. The usual shape of this file is a
# deny list, which gets the default wrong: anything a future commit adds to the
# tree is in the build context until someone remembers to exclude it. Here the
# default is exclusion, so a new directory is invisible to the build until it is
# named below.
#
# That matters more than build speed. The build context is uploaded to the Docker
# daemon in full, whether or not a COPY ever references it, and this tree has an
# in-repo `.demo-workspace/`, agent worktrees under `.claude/`, a `.venv/` and a
# `.snakemake/` cache. None of them belong anywhere near an image build.
#
# THE FIXTURE RULES AT THE BOTTOM ARE THE POINT. The two synthetic fixtures are
# the only genomic files the image contains, and they are fully fabricated
# (fictional `SYNTH*` gene symbols). `tests/` is re-included only so those two
# paths can be, and then its contents are excluded again so that no other VCF,
# BAM, CRAM or FASTQ can reach the context -- including one that does not exist
# yet. Patient data is bind-mounted at runtime and never built in (ADR 0006,
# GP-40); see workflow/containers/README.md.
# =============================================================================

# --- deny everything --------------------------------------------------------
*

# --- what the Dockerfile copies ---------------------------------------------
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!Snakefile
!src
!config
!knowledge
!workflow
!templates

# Bind-mounted at build time by the demo-parity assertion, not copied into the
# image. Still has to be in the context to be mountable.
!justfile

# --- the two synthetic fixtures, and nothing else under tests/ --------------
!tests
tests/*
!tests/fixtures
tests/fixtures/*
!tests/fixtures/synthetic
tests/fixtures/synthetic/*
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/synthetic_case.vcf
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/synthetic_phenotype.tsv

# --- belt and braces --------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing above re-includes these, so these lines are redundant by construction.
# They are here so that a later edit which loosens the allowlist -- say, swapping
# `!src` for `!*` in a hurry -- still cannot sweep in credentials or a workspace.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.demo-workspace
**/runs
